    #strong[Dynamic reconfigurability for hybrid analog-digital quantum simulation.] #strong[a,] Hybrid quantum circuit combining coherent atom transport with analog Hamiltonian evolution and digital quantum gates. #strong[b,] Measuring entanglement entropy in a many-body Rydberg system via two-copy interferometry. #strong[c,] Measured half-chain Renyi entanglement entropy after many-body dynamics following quenches on two 8-atom systems. Quenching from $|"gggg…" ⟩$ ($|g ⟩ equiv |1 ⟩$) results in rapid entropy growth and saturation, signifying quantum thermalization. Quenching from $|"rgrg…" ⟩$ reveals a significantly slower growth of entanglement entropy. #strong[d,] Measuring the mutual information at 0.5-μs quench time reveals a volume-law scaling for the thermalizing $|"gggg…" ⟩$ state, and an area-law scaling for the scarring $|"rgrg…" ⟩$ state. #strong[e,] The single-site Renyi entropies for sites in the middle of the chain quickly increase and saturate for the $|"gggg…" ⟩$ quench, but show large oscillations for the $|"rgrg…" ⟩$ quench. Solid curves are results of exact numerical simulations for the isolated quantum system under $H_"Ryd"$ with no free parameters (see Methods for details of data processing). Error bars represent 1 standard deviation.
  ]
) <fig:fig4>
