iagram of the constrained Hilbert space of the system @Turner2018. The early-time, out-of-phase entropy oscillations @Ho2019 of the scars can be understood in this constrained Hilbert space picture, where the scar dynamics are known to take the state from the left end ($|"rgrgrgrg" ⟩$) to the right end ($|"grgrgrgr" ⟩$) (dark circles represent $|r ⟩$ and white circles represent $|g ⟩$) @Turner2018. Near these crystalline ends of this constrained Hilbert space, the Rydberg atoms can fluctuate (high entropy), but the ground state atoms are pinned (low entropy). Our analysis shows that entanglement between atoms on the same sublattice contributes to the eventual degradation of the revival fidelity of the $|bb(Z)_2 ⟩$ state.
